    <Replace Tag="LOC_SDP_STATES_TOOLTIP" Language="en_US">
      <Text>Must: always placed. Pool: when the count is above the required number, the best of the pool are picked. Off: left out. Districts are compared by weighted adjacency (plus land, coverage and distance when on), so districts without adjacency (encampment, aerodrome) are never picked from the pool: make them Must. Districts limited to one per empire (government plaza) are Must or Off only.</Text>
    </Replace>
    <Replace Tag="LOC_SDP_STATES_OTHER_TOOLTIP" Language="en_US">
      <Text>These districts need no population and do not count. Auto: added when the city needs it, placed by the solver. An aqueduct when the city lacks fresh water (housing from water below the 5 of a river or lake); a dam when three or more floodplain plots in its rings are free (Gathering Storm). Left out, with a note, when it fits nowhere.</Text>
